Article 36 (Designation of Fire Equipment Maintenance Center) (1) The Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency may designate an institution or organization satisfying requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as professional human resources and facilities, etc., as a fire equipment maintenance center (hereinafter referred to as “Center”) for systematic, professional and efficient maintenance of fire equipment.
  (2) The Center shall conduct the following affairs:
  1. Examination of fire equipment;
  2. Inspection and maintenance of fire equipment;
  3. Tasks entrusted by the State, local governments or public institutions in relation to examination, inspection and maintenance, etc. of fire equipment;
  4. Other tasks prescribed by Presidential Decree to achieve the purpose of the establishment of the Center.
  (3) The Mayor/Do Governor may designate an individual or an organization that meets the requirements determined and publicly notified by the Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency, such as professional human resources and facilities, as a fire engine maintenance business establishment (hereinafter referred to as "business establishment") to inspect and maintain fire engines under his or her jurisdiction. <Newly Inserted on Nov. 15, 2022>
  (4) Where a person designated as the Center pursuant to paragraph (1) or a business establishment pursuant to paragraph (3) falls under any of the following, the Commissioner of the National Fire Agency or the Mayor/Do Governor may order the revocation of its designation or the suspension of operation of its affairs for a specific period not exceeding six months, as prescribed by Presidential Decree: Provided, That in cases falling under subparagraph 1, the Commissioner of the National Fire Agency or the Mayor/Do Governor shall revoke its designation: <Amended on Nov. 15, 2022>
  1. Where it has been designated by fraud or other improper means;
  2. Where it has failed to conduct its affairs for six months or longer without good cause;
  3. Where it has failed to satisfy the requirements for designation under paragraph (1) or (3).
  (5) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (4), matters necessary for the designation and operation of the Center or business establishments and other necessary matters shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree. <Amended on Nov. 15, 2022>
